Screen
/ PlangOS's shell: part of the system (plang's os folder, read-only, comes with the image), run in
/ the person's app, /home/plang — their files, their .db. Host plang starts it (wsl … --cd
/ /home/plang … /opt/plang/plang system/plangos/Screen).
/ PlangOS's side of the screen. The
/ screen is PlangOS's display: programs draw onto it, and its frames go to this app's output —
/ the pipe to host plang. Input from the host comes down on stdin, one line per event, and goes
/ to the screen. Ends when the host closes the pipe.
/ The first page is the desktop; every app opens in a window of its own.
- screen.open(ToOutput=true, OnWindow=goal.call(Name="Window")); variable.set(Name=%screen%, Value=%!data%)
- browser.start(Url="file:///opt/plang/os/system/plangos/desktop.html", Screen=%screen%, OnMessage=goal.call(Name="Desktop")); variable.set(Name=%browser%, Value=%!data%)
/ A question for the user (a permission, `ask user "…"`) is a dialog on the screen: asked on the
/ console, it would go into the screen's pipe and wait on the host's input.
- channel.set(Name="input", Goal=goal.call(Name="Question"))
/ The screen takes the host's input itself — no goal per event, so nothing waits behind a goal
/ (a question waiting for the click that answers it).
- screen.listen(Screen=%screen%)
- stop %browser%

Question
/ The question in a dialog on the desktop, lifted above every window; the answer is what the person
/ chose (a permission: y, a or n; a question: what they typed). The question is %message%.
- window.callGoal(Name="AskShow", Window=%browser.desktop%, Parameter={question: %message%}); variable.set(Name=%above%, Value=%!data%)
- send %above% to %screen%
- window.callGoal(Name="AskAnswer", Window=%browser.desktop%); variable.set(Name=%answer%, Value=%!data%)
- send %answer.below% to %screen%
- return %answer.text%

Desktop
/ The desktop page asks: {"open": url} opens a window; {"window": "focus|minimize|…", "id"}
/ goes to the screen; {"files"} shows the desktop's files; {"edit": path} opens one in Writer.
/ Writer asks: {"save": path, "text"}, {"list": folder}, {"load": path}, {"create": path},
/ {"build": path}, {"run": goal}; "from" is the window that asked.
- set %asked% to %!data%
- if %asked.open%, call Open
- if %asked.window%, call Command
- if %asked.files%, call Files
- if %asked.edit%, call Edit
- if %asked.save%, call Save
- if %asked.list%, call List
- if %asked.load%, call Load
- if %asked.create%, call Create
- if %asked.build%, call Build
- if %asked.run%, call Run

Open
- open window %asked.open% in %browser%

Command
- send %asked% to %screen%

Files
/ the desktop's files: what is in the app's Desktop/, shown as icons. A path that starts with "/"
/ is in the app (/home/plang); without it, it would be beside this goal, in the os folder.
- list files in '/Desktop', write to %files%
- call ShowFiles files=%files% in %browser.desktop%

Edit
/ a file opens in Writer, in a window of its own: what it holds — a text file its text, a json file
/ its value
- open window 'file:///opt/plang/os/system/plangos/app/writer/start.html' in %browser%, write to %writer%
- read %asked.edit%, write to %content%
- call Show file=%asked.edit%, content=%content% in %writer%

Save
/ Ctrl+S in Writer: the file's format writes what Writer sends — a text file's text, a json file's value
- save %asked.content% to %asked.save%
- window.callGoal(Name="Saved", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%)

List
/ Writer's Open and New: the files in a folder and its folders
- list files in %asked.list% recursive, write to %files%
- window.callGoal(Name="ShowList", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={folder: %asked.list%, files: %files%})

Load
/ Writer's Open: another file in the same window
- read %asked.load%, write to %content%
- window.callGoal(Name="Show", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={file: %asked.load%, content: %content%})

Create
/ Writer's New: an empty file, opened in the same window; the desktop shows it
- file.save(Path=%asked.create%, Value="")
- window.callGoal(Name="Show", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={file: %asked.create%, content: ""})
- call Files

Build
/ Writer's ▶ (build): plang builds the app — its own process, as plang build does anywhere; what it
/ wrote, and how it ended, go back to the window.
- terminal.start(App="plang", Parameter=["build", "--llmservice=openai"]); on.timeout(After="PT10M"); on.error(Recovery=[goal.call(Name="BuildFailed")]); variable.set(Name=%built%, Value=%!data%)
- window.callGoal(Name="Built", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={output: %built%, error: %built!error%, code: %built!exitCode%})

BuildFailed
/ plang couldn't be started (or timed out): the window hears it, rather than waiting on
- window.callGoal(Name="Built", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={error: %!error.Message%, code: -1})

Run
/ Writer's ▶ (run): the goal runs in a plang of its own (this one's output is the screen); what it
/ wrote goes back to the window.
- terminal.start(App="plang", Parameter=[%asked.run%]); on.timeout(After="PT5M"); on.error(Recovery=[goal.call(Name="RunFailed")]); variable.set(Name=%ran%, Value=%!data%)
- window.callGoal(Name="Ran", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={output: %ran%, error: %ran!error%, code: %ran!exitCode%})

RunFailed
- window.callGoal(Name="Ran", Window=%asked.from%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={error: %!error.Message%, code: -1})

Window
/ The screen says what happened to a window: the desktop's taskbar shows it. Enter in a
/ window's address field ({"navigate": what was typed, "id"}) sends that window there; its
/ menu's New window, and links opened as tabs ({"open": url}), open a window.
- set %event% to %!data%
- post %event% to %browser.desktop%
- if %event.navigate%, call Navigate
- if %event.open%, call OpenPage
- if %event.tool%, call Tool
- if %event.paste%, call Paste

Navigate
- navigate window %event.id% to %event.navigate% in %browser%

OpenPage
- open window %event.open% in %browser%

Tool
/ One of the app's tools in its window's title bar was clicked ({"tool": "save", "id"}): its page's
/ goal Tool gets it. The page named its tools itself ({"window": "tools", "tools": [...]}).
- window.callGoal(Name="Tool", Window=%event.id%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={tool: %event.tool%})

Paste
/ A page asked for the clipboard as a value ({"window": "paste"}): a copy that knows where it came
/ from, as json; its page's goal Paste gets it.
- window.callGoal(Name="Paste", Window=%event.id%, Browser=%browser%, Parameter={value: %event.paste%})
